<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Komercni Banka details Q1 results.</title>
<headline>Czech Komercni Banka details Q1 results.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The largest Czech bank Komercni Banka a.s. said on Wednesday it had posted lower first quarter 1997 profits according to both international and Czech accounting standards.</p>
<p>Results for period ending March 31, 1997 according to international accounting standards and subsequently according to Czech accounting standards (in billions of crowns).</p>
<p>INTERNATIONAL ACCOUNTING STANDARDS</p>
<p>				  Q1 1997	vs	Q1 1996</p>
<p> Total assets		 443.919		  397.987</p>
<p> Total net revenue	    4.929		    5.092</p>
<p>profit before provision</p>
<p> for loan losses		2.414		    2.419</p>
<p> provision for loan losses  1.371		    1.071</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit		 1.043		    1.348</p>
<p> Taxation			     0			  0</p>
<p> After tax profit	     1.043		    1.348</p>
<p>CZECH ACCOUNTING STANDARDS</p>
<p>				  Q1 1997	 vs	Q1 1996</p>
<p> Total assets		456.539		    414.272</p>
<p> Equity			  9.503			9.503</p>
<p> Interest income	    10.168			8.931</p>
<p> Interest expense	    6.940			5.694</p>
<p> General operating costs   2.061			1.811</p>
<p>Depreciation and provisions for tangible</p>
<p> and intangible assets     0.320			0.274</p>
<p>Creation of reserves and</p>
<p> provisions for loans	1.682			1.212</p>
<p>Application of reserves</p>
<p> and provisions for loans  0.408			0.018</p>
<p> After tax profit	    0.868			1.360</p>
<p>-- Robin Shepherd, Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
